      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we updated these makers to first call `GlyphVector::MakeFromBuffer`, calculate the bounds, and then pass that to `VertexFiller::MakeFromBuffer` we wouldn\u0027t have to do a late reconstruct modification.\n\nSince the bounds of the GlyphVector share code inside this compilation unit, we could have `SubRun::MakeFromBuffer` first load the glyph vector and calculate bounds (working out to a no-op for path and drawable subruns), and then pass the vector and the bounds to `MakeFromBuffer`.\n\nOne additional thing I noticed was that the `MakeFromBuffer` functions are nearly identical between the atlas sub runs. The few extra parameters that they do have should also probably not be serialized, but instead re-derived from the positionMatrix passed to canBeReused or re-derived from the creation matrix.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1013,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1017,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "852395b2e2a2cf49f3b8a3a207e0d8845182d12f",
